 "text": "Hi, how have you been? That's a great choice for a picnic buddy. Which part are you nervous about? Okay. What's the message about? That's enough. Keep the leash in one hand so you can quickly clip it on. You' got today to practice and pack. A short trial walk in the park helps too. Call from a quiet spot with the leash in his harness, not his mouth. Much better. Now clip the harness on and let him smell his collar. Then take the harness off and try tomorrow. Running from him will take several days to regain his trust.",
